  "id": "COMPOUND:1787 - PROTEIN:3990",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanistic link between 3,4-Dihydroxycinnamic Acid and the Inner centromere protein, through multiple indirect pathways. The drug is implicated in targeting several entities that ultimately interact with the Inner centromere protein, including MGC-803, 3 beta-hydroxysteroid dehydrogenase/Delta 5-->4-isomerase type 1, and Penicillin-binding protein 1A. These targets are involved in distinct biochemical processes, yet all converge toward the Inner centromere protein, indicating a possible coordinated regulatory role. The integration of these pathways implies that 3,4-Dihydroxycinnamic Acid may exert its effects through a complex network of molecular interactions that ultimately modulate the function of the Inner centromere protein. The evidence supports a mechanistic connection, though the exact nature of the interactions remains to be fully elucidated.",
